title: SeventhBall
---
<<hideBatsman>>
<<if $selection == "None">>
    <<moveDialogue top>>
    <<showCharacterImage center>>
    <<resetToOriginalPresets>>
    Ramu: Timer's getting tighter—adapt quickly!
<<elseif $selection == "PullShotNormal">>
    <<resetToOriginalPresets>>
    <<moveDialogue top>>
    <<showCharacterImage center>>
    Ramu: Captain, Watch the line of the ball. A cut shot is more suited for this delivery.
<<elseif $selection == "CutShotNormal" || $selection == "CutShotLofted">>
    <<resetToOriginalPresets>>
    <<moveDialogue top>>
    <<showCharacterImage center>>
    Ramu: Good adaptation—cut shots work for short balls outside off.
<<elseif $selection == "ForwardDefense">>
    <<resetToOriginalPresets>>
    <<moveDialogue top>>
    <<showCharacterImage center>>
    Ramu: Careful—forward defense is risky against bouncers. Duck or play back.
<<elseif $selection == "Leave">>
    <<resetToOriginalPresets>>
    <<moveDialogue top>>
    <<showCharacterImage center>>
    Ramu: Smart choice—sometimes leaving is the best option.
<<else>>
    <<resetToOriginalPresets>>
    <<moveDialogue top>>
    <<showCharacterImage center>>
    Ramu: Short balls need horizontal bat shots or ducking.
<<endif>>
<<resetToOriginalPresets>>
<<moveDialogue top>>
<<showCharacterImage center>>
Ramu: Good practice with the timer. Now let's learn about the Redraw button.
<<ballFourthBall>>
<<unhideBallerCard>>
<<showFlipButton>>
Ramu: None of these shots are ideal. Time to Redraw—press the button.
<<hideCharacterImage>>
